-- --opens specification (seg/WRITING.md, rule 6) for MapFib
-- (doc/mapping-fib.pdf): one entry per declaration.  Generated from --opened
-- (28 Oct 2026); the openings were checked against the note by kind (below), not entry by entry.
-- Kinds as in fibre.opens; in addition:
--   by-definition steps of the text: (L ; q)_1 = \ x -> (L x).1 and
--     (p ; G)_1 = G_1 o p_1 (ptcomp, fpr, fpt; Fib, Triple.F/f0) in uniq,
--     ext-eq, inj-at, fseq, chain, right, s-eq; a . refl is a (Prelude.trans)
--     in cancel-snd, g-def; fib-fst (W.fib, subst on refl); Ex, Un, U0 are
--     the hypotheses (E), (U), (U0); Phi is [kappa ; KMap.K four] (g-eq);
--     H4 is isEquiv of Phi (g, g-eq, s); e1inv is the map of pt-inv e1
--     (psi-equiv, Definition 16); Psi (psi-equiv); Unloop, isContr (LoopEq.equiv);
--     Bij.equiv opens Bijection.Injective;
--   the carrier HC opened to Quot.Q and its image (surj, inj, s, rep-fib, right):
--     extra (ii) of doc/pi3-s2-postnikov.pdf;
--   sigma-nat: the base point of a looping (Maps.D, Kf, idJR): extra (i)
--     of doc/pi3-s2-postnikov.pdf, used in the types of loop-comp;
--   K(Z,2) as a type (KZ2 -> KK.K two -> EMSpace.K -> ... -> Deloop.Torsors.Tor)
--     in cp: the etaV mechanism of fibre.opens, not a step of the text;
--   index arithmetic of cor11 (NatArith.plus, isConn, isTrunc, numerals).
-- Check: segd All.seg --opens mapfib.opens ; every line "nothing else opened".
